lean.nvim (MIT)
---------------

This project is an independent Vim9 port modeled after lean.nvim:

  https://github.com/Julian/lean.nvim

The port was built against lean.nvim commit
e05c0f821412337259b98cc732ff0cf6ac7afe0c. The following files are copied
byte-for-byte from that revision under lean.nvim's MIT license:

  data/lean/snippets.json
  snippets/lean.json

syntax/lean.vim is copied from the same revision with one local change: the
global markdown highlight overrides (hi! link markdownCodeBlock/markdownError)
were removed because they restyled Markdown buffers outside Lean sessions.

The following Vim9 files translate or adapt portions of lean.nvim's behavior
or implementation and are also distributed under the MIT license:

  autoload/lean/abbreviations.vim
  ftplugin/lean.vim
  indent/lean.vim

The October 2026 update also adapts lean.nvim's infoview folding and
sign-column defaults from commits:

  718540c8081bc6c8d9485d8c407b40e6c5c01468
  d90c91bf150652e3710c8e00ab4d4a316f8593b8

These affect ftplugin/leaninfo.vim, autoload/lean/infoview.vim, and
ftplugin/lean.vim and are distributed under the same MIT license.

The wider plugin follows lean.nvim's public commands, mappings, feature
organization, and editor behavior. See ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md for fuller credit.

